To create a simple toast notification using React Context, follow these steps:

1. Create a `ToastContext` file:

```javascript
import React from 'react';

const ToastContext = React.createContext();

function ToastProvider({ children }) {
  const [toasts, setToasts] = React.useState([]);

  function addToast(message) {
    setToasts((prevToasts) => [...prevToasts, message]);
  }

  return (
    <ToastContext.Provider value={{ toasts, addToast }}>
      {children}
    </ToastContext.Provider>
  );
}

export { ToastContext, ToastProvider };
```

2. Create a `Toast` component:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { useContext } from 'react';

function Toast() {
  const { toasts } = useContext(ToastContext);

  return (
    <div className="toast-container">
      {toasts.map((toast) => (
        <div key={toast} className="toast">{toast}</div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}

export default Toast;
```

3. Use the `ToastProvider` and `Toast` components in your application:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { ToastContext, ToastProvider, Toast } from './ToastContext';

function App() {
  return (
    <ToastProvider>
      <Toast />
      {/* Add toast messages here */}
      <button onClick={() => setToasts([...toasts, 'New toast message'])}>Add Toast</button>
    </ToastProvider>
  );
}

export default App;
```

In this example, we've created a `ToastContext` that provides a `toasts` array and an `addToast` function to add new toast messages. The `Toast` component renders the list of toast messages. You can use the `ToastProvider` and `Toast` components in your application to display toast notifications.

