4. Use `useState` to manage the `editedName` and `editedPrompt` states, which will reduce the number of times the state is updated and improve performance.
5. Use `useRef` to cache the `selectedTargetPrompt` ref, which will prevent unnecessary re-creation of the ref and improve performance.
6. Use `useIntersectionObserver` to lazy-load the prompts list, which will reduce the initial load time and improve performance.
7. Use `useDebounce` to debounce the input field changes, which will reduce the number of times the API is called and improve performance.
8. Use `useThrottle` to throttle the modal close event, which will reduce the number of times the API is called and improve performance.

